{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-rev-5-1","title":"Revelation 5:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 The book sealed with seven seals, 9 which only the Lamb that was slain is worthy to open. 12 Therefore the elders praise him, and confess that he redeemed them with his blood.</p>\n<p>that sat. 4:3 a book. 10:2,8-11; Isa 34:16; Eze 2:9,10 sealed. 6:1; Isa 8:16; 29:11; Da 8:26; 12:4-9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-2","title":"Revelation 5:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>a strong. Ps 103:20 Who. 5:5; Isa 29:11,12; 41:22,23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-3","title":"Revelation 5:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>13; Isa 40:13,14; 41:28; Ro 11:34</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-4","title":"Revelation 5:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>because. 4:1; Da 12:8,9</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-5","title":"Revelation 5:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>one. 4:4,10; 7:13 Weep. Jer 31:16; Lu 7:13; 8:52; 23:28; Joh 20:13 the Lion. Ge 49:9,10; Nu 24:9; Heb 7:14 the Root. 22:16; Isa 11:1,10; Jer 23:5,6; Ro 1:3; 15:12 hath. 1:1; 6:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-6","title":"Revelation 5:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>in the midst of the throne. 4:4-6 a Lamb.An emblematical representation of our Saviour's high priesthood.</p>\n<p>9,12; 6:16; 7:9-17; 12:11; 13:8; 17:14; 21:23; 22:1,3; Isa 53:7,8 Joh 1:29,36; Ac 8:32; 1Pe 1:19,20 seven horns.As a horn is the emblem of power, and seven the number of perfection, the seven horns may denote the almighty power of Jesus Christ.</p>\n<p>1Sa 2:10; Da 7:14; Mic 4:13; Hab 3:4; Lu 1:69; Php 2:9-11 seven eyes.His infinite knowledge and wisdom; and especially \"the treasures of wisdom\" laid up in him, to be communicated to the Church by \"the seven spirits of God\", i.e., the Holy Spirit.</p>\n<p>2Ch 16:9; Zec 3:9; 4:10 the seven spirits. 4:5</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-7","title":"Revelation 5:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":7,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":7},"content":"<p>out. 1; 4:2,3</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-8","title":"Revelation 5:8","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":8,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":8},"content":"<p>the four. 14; 4:4,8,10; 7:10-12; 19:4; Joh 5:23; Ro 14:10-12; Php 2:9-11 Heb 1:6 having. 14:2,3; 15:2; Ps 33:2; 43:4; 81:2; 150:3 golden. 15:7 odours. or incense. the prayers. 8:3,4; Ps 141:2</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-9","title":"Revelation 5:9","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":9,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":9},"content":"<p>sung. 7:10-12; 14:3; Ps 33:3; 40:3; 96:1; 98:1; 144:9; 149:1; Isa 42:10 Thou art. 2,3; 4:11 for. 6,12; 13:8 and hast. 14:4,6; Mt 20:28; 26:28; Ac 20:28; Ro 3:24-26; 1Co 6:20; 7:23 Eph 1:7; Col 1:14; Tit 2:14; Heb 11:14; 1Pe 1:18,19; 2Pe 2:1 1Jo 1:7; 2:2 out. 7:9; 11:9; 14:6; Da 4:1; 6:25; Mr 16:15,16; Col 1:23</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-10","title":"Revelation 5:10","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":10,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":10},"content":"<p>kings. 1:6; 20:6; 22:5; Ex 19:6; 1Pe 2:5-9 we. 20:6; Da 7:18,27</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-11","title":"Revelation 5:11","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":11,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":11},"content":"<p>many. 7:11; 1Ki 22:19; 2Ki 6:16-18; Ps 103:20; 148:2 the throne. 4:4,6,9,10 was. 19:6; De 33:2; Ps 68:17; Da 7:10; Heb 12:22</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-12","title":"Revelation 5:12","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":12,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":12},"content":"<p>Worthy. 9; Zec 13:7 to receive. 4:11; 7:12; 19:1; Mt 28:18; Joh 3:35,36; 17:2; 2Co 8:9; Php 2:9-11 1Ti 1:17</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-13","title":"Revelation 5:13","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":13,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":13},"content":"<p>every. 3; 7:9,10; Ps 96:11-13; 148:2-13; Lu 2:14; Php 2:10; Col 1:23 such. Isa 24:14; 42:10 blessing. 12; 1:6; 1Ch 29:11; Ps 72:18,19; Mt 6:13; Ro 9:5; 11:36; 16:27 Eph 3:21; 1Ti 4:16; 1Pe 4:11; 5:11; Jude 1:25 him. 4:2,3 and unto. 6,9; 6:16; 7:10</p>"},{"id":"tsk-rev-5-14","title":"Revelation 5:14","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"REV","chapterStart":5,"verseStart":14,"chapterEnd":5,"verseEnd":14},"content":"<p>the four. 19:4 And the four and. 4:9-11</p>"}]}